argeter found a few strands of hair caught on the railings near 67 Wentworth Street: the culprit is grey-haired.","Henry Pargeter's housekeeper swears Henry Pargeter was at home all that evening and never went out until breakfast.","The boot-boy in Henry Pargeter's house swears Henry Pargeter was at home all that evening and never went out until breakfast."],"bribe":["The publican saw Henry Pargeter hand a sovereign each to three of Henry Pargeter's own servants the morning after, saying 'and mind you all tell it the same way.'","A bank clerk says Henry Pargeter drew twenty pounds in sovereigns at opening time the day after the murder; by noon Henry Pargeter's household staff were all wearing new boots."],"planted":"By the body lies a small silver snuff-box. Odd: it is bone-dry, though rain fell until three in the morning and everything else on the step is soaked.","holmes":"Wiggins, Pargeter's servants supply both his alibi and evidence against Leopold; the dry snuff-box suggests planting. Pargeter merits suspicion, not accusation."}}